        "severity": "error",
        "problem": "The qualification that limits the headline — \"Two teams, eight weeks. Quality and error rates were not measured.\" — is set at 25 px in light gray as a caption beneath the chart, smaller and weaker than the 29 px body text and far weaker than the 50 px bold headline \"Review time fell from 40 to 16 hours\". A reader skimming the headline can take the speed gain at face value while the missing quality/error measurement, which is the whole reason a decision is needed, reads as a footnote.",
